course: dictionary
lesson: 2851
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one the writer means. The word dog is a good example. «The dog barked.» means an animal kept as a pet. But «The team was dogged by bad luck» uses dog as a verb, and it means followed closely or kept troubled by something.
explain: Look at the clues. In «A dog that growls, shows its teeth or goes stiff is warning you to stay away», the dog is a real animal, and growls and shows its teeth tell you how to behave around it. Always ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then test it.
explain: Writers in science and formal texts often use other words for dog. You might meet canine, which means the same thing. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: A dog is an animal kept as a pet or for work, and it has 4 legs.
fact: Wild dogs include wolves, foxes and dingoes.
fact: As a verb, to dog someone means to follow them closely, or to keep troubling them: «dogged by bad luck».
fact: «Dog-tired» means very tired.
fact: In formal writing, dog can be called «canine», «domestic dog» or «Canis familiaris».
exercise: «The dog barked.» In this sentence, what is a dog? | A kind of weather | A mess in the kitchen | *A pet animal that barks and wags its tail
exercise: Ben says, «The team was dogged by bad luck all season.» What does dogged mean here? | Given a bath and brushed | Barked at loudly | *Followed closely and kept troubled by something
exercise: «A dog that growls, shows its teeth or goes stiff is warning you to stay away.» Find and copy one word that shows the dog is warning you. | *growls | runs | yawns | sleeps
test: Which formal word means the same as dog? | *canine | bovine | feline | equine
test: Mia says, «I am dog-tired after the walk.» What does she mean? | *She is very tired | She is wide awake and full of energy | She has a dog to walk | She is very hungry
exam: «Each canine consumes two bowls of food a day.» What is a canine in this sentence? | A bird | *A dog | A cat | A fish
